; The large font. One pixel is one column by half a row; `#` is ink.
;
; A capital is `cap` pixels tall: five rows, two-pixel strokes both ways, so
; every bar lands on a whole row. Lowercase has a six-pixel x-height, which
; leaves exactly room for an accent above it inside the capitals' rows. A
; letter with a descender gives `cap + descent` rows; anything else gives
; `cap` and the descender rows are blank.
;
; Accented letters are not drawn here. They are composed from the base letter
; and a `mark:`, which is centred over the letter `gap` pixels above its ink.

cap 10
descent 4
gap 2
space 4
tracking 1

